                <pb facs="0967" n="951" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg951"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 55D128: Black Book, Tab 94: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, Far East</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ridgway</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Joint
                        Chiefs of Staff </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-26T16:41:00+09:00">26 September
                            1951—4:41 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>ZX–39742. Fol rel to press simultaneously Tokyo and CINCUNC Adv 1700 local this
                    date: The United Nations Command liaison officers met with the Communist liaison
                    officers at Kaesong at 1000 hours today. The Communist liaison officers proposed
                    a meeting of the delegates at 1000 hours 27 Sep, which proposal was answered by
                    the United Nations Command liaison officers that their instructions were to meet
                    with Communist liaison officers to discuss conditions mutually satisfactory
                    prior to the resumption of conference discussions by the delegations.</p>
                <p>The meeting of the liaison officers was recessed by mutual agreement at 1120
                    hours.</p>
            </div>
